# In-game diplomacy / players overlay (toggled during play, the game keeps running, so no scrim): the box window is a
# 1200 x 760 dialog centred (x 360..1560, y 160..920): column titles, one row per player (mute mark as the stock icon,
# name, side, team, status), the close button bottom-right. The three containers (in-game, solo, buddies) are moved over
# the dialog first; only the in-game one is shown in a skirmish or LAN game. Units: 1 = frame height / 1080.
window $Parent centre middle 0 0 1200 760 dialog
window $InGameParent left top 360 160 1200 760
hide $InGameParent
window $SoloParent left top 360 160 1200 760
hide $SoloParent
window $BuddiesParent left top 360 160 1200 760
hide $BuddiesParent
# in a solo game the code shows the solo container instead of the player rows: its list fills the same area; the
# buddies container (online only) gets the same treatment so nothing stock-drawn can show; the mode radios stay hidden
window $ListboxSolo left top 384 232 1152 600 list
window $ListboxBuddies left top 384 232 1152 360 list
window $ListboxBuddyChat left top 384 608 1152 200 list
window $TextEntryChat left top 384 816 900 40 entry
hide $RadioButtonInGame
hide $RadioButtonBuddies

window $StaticTextMuteTitle left top 384 184 60 24 meta
window $StaticTextPlayerTitle left top 432 184 300 24 meta
window $StaticTextSideTitle left top 756 184 400 24 meta
window $StaticTextTeamTitle left top 1180 184 100 24 meta
window $StaticTextStatusTitle left top 1300 184 220 24 meta
rule left top 384 216 1152

